  },
  "limitations": "One agent and one behaviour per call; no behaviour blending, obstacle avoidance, separation or wander (wander is random). Pursuit assumes a straight-moving evader in this simulation. Steering ignores walls: in the game, collisions (G004) push NPCs out of buildings.",
  "port_notes": "2D port of Yuka's 3D vector maths on the x-z plane (Yuka y=0). Direction (getDirection) is modelled as the normalised last displacement, which is what Vehicle.update sets through lookAt when speed^2 > 1e-8; before any movement it is the given heading, the velocity direction, or Yuka's forward +z. A single behaviour with weight 1 passes through SteeringManager._accumulate. Smoother is not used (Yuka default null).",
  "flow_role": "Step 4 (NPC ve polis davranışı): tune pedestrian arrive (walking between route waypoints), traffic seek and police pursuit; check that police at the chosen speed can catch a car that stops but not one at full speed. The JavaScript runtime in G012 uses the same formulas; the end-to-end test compares them."
}
